    "message": "Let each independent queue's head wait without breaking the stall check\n\nA water or meal station with one queue per service point records why a\nqueue's head waits, but WorldState.validate accepted only the head of\nthe facility-wide projection, so a stall at the second queue's head\nstopped the simulation. The check and the stale-stall cleanup now\naccept the head of any of the facility's queues.\n\nRecording each queue's stall in turn also swapped the facility's record\nevery minute while two queues waited, logging the same waits again and\nrecounting the stall reasons shown as KPIs. The station now keeps a\nhead's record while it still waits for the same reason, and otherwise\nrecords the first stalled queue in queue ID order. The saved state\nkeeps its shape.\n\nThe test setup that stands three people at a facility moves to\ntests/conftest.py so the new unit test can use it (#118).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
